# Blackjack Roulette — Game Design & Technical Specification

> Working title: **Blackjack Roulette**
> Genre: Multiplayer turn-based strategy / survival
> Platform: Web (primary), wrapped as native app later via Capacitor
> Prototype scope: 4 players, single match, no persistence beyond a session

This document is written to be handed directly to an AI coding assistant (Cursor) as a build spec. It contains the full game design, data model, networking contract, and UI/visual direction needed to scaffold and implement the prototype.

---

## 1. High Concept

A multiplayer strategy game combining **Blackjack** rounds with a **Russian Roulette** survival twist. Every round, the lowest-scoring player risks elimination. Players hold a small inventory of items that let them manipulate their odds — in the cards, and in the chamber.

**One-line pitch:** *Buckshot Roulette meets the blackjack table.*

## 2. Design Pillars

- **High tension** — every round has real stakes; someone is always one bad pull from being out.
- **Easy to learn** — blackjack rules are near-universal; roulette add-on is a single extra concept.
- **Constant player interaction** — items target other players, turns are visible to the table, nobody tunes out.
- **Short matches** — under 15 minutes per match, so players naturally ask for a rematch.

## 3. Success Metric (validate before adding scope)

The ONLY thing this prototype needs to prove: **players feel clever moments (not just pure chance), and ask for a rematch.**

Do not add new items, cosmetics, or systems until this is validated with real playtesters. This spec deliberately stays scoped to the MVP loop.

